        "like": 12
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Seeing as a lot of games have this, and similar programs such as IMVU and the likes also have this, I don't think it's a bad idea at all and there's to be honest not really anything to complain about.\n\nSome alternatives to how it could be done though would be that if having the ingame request isn't possible, then perhaps it could be done on the website by having one person signing a marriage request and then sending it to another user and they have to accept it for it to be completed.\n\nThen ingame as the OP said, there would be some sort of unique visual showing that a person is married, and preferably to whom they are married.\nAnd getting divorced would be as simple as just one person selecting they want a divorce and it would cancel the status. To be fair and right, of course. Otherwise you may find a situation where one person is denying every divorce request which forces the other person to contact devs and it would create a huge scene.\n\nThat said, i'd give this 10 votes if i could xD",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
